    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup faces a slate defined by high-ceiling matchups against middle-tier arms, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (75.13) and **Jacob Wilson** (72.17). **Kyle Tucker** serves as our primary anchor today; facing Brandon Pfaadt, he benefits from a favorable park environment and a massive boost in expectation due to the pitcher\u2019s skill profile. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** receives a significant efficiency lift from a rare combination of positive park factors and a plus-matchup against a lefty starter, solidifying his status as a high-floor play despite the volatility of the #2 spot. **Andy Pages** also thrives in this same Pfaadt matchup, with his efficiency bolstered by an 86% stolen base success rate against a starter known for slow delivery, providing the speed-category upside necessary for our 5x5 Roto standing.\n\nWe are navigating significant risk against elite arms today, specifically with **Gunnar Henderson** (61.80) and **Heliot Ramos** (50.03), both of whom are tethered to sub-3.30 xERA pitchers in Jacob deGrom and Chris Sale. While **Gunnar Henderson** maintains elite standing due to a 14% platoon adjustment, his score is actively suppressed by deGrom\u2019s ability to neutralize base-stealing attempts. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Sam Antonacci** (43.59), who fell just shy of the starting threshold. Despite his aggressive #1 spot in the projected order, the optimizer preferred the superior matchup profile of **Wade Meckler** (54.57), as **Sam Antonacci** is forced to contend with Gavin Williams\u2019 sub-3.00 xERA. As we monitor pending lineups for **Liam Hicks**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill**, we must remain alert; any late-breaking shifts in the batting order could necessitate a pivot to our bench depth, specifically **Luis Lara** or **Miguel Vargas**, to protect our daily game caps.",
